ackage damage, or abandoned temporary artifacts were observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-21ea9ab10a494dc0","cmd-e06f83999ac44a3d","cmd-3d258acf42e54e6e","cmd-8ca0dd2c177749d8","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. curl remained at its original version despite a directly tested upgrade path, while the operating-system release and kernel were retained. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also complete: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered running state with zero failed units, and persistence of curl, its lock, the OS release, and the kernel were directly observed and independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["Validation used a targeted `dnf upgrade curl` rather than executing an unrestricted whole-system update; however, candidate checks with and without the active version-lock plugin directly demonstrate that the newer curl build is excluded by the lock.","The single-node topology has no separate application data or cluster state to validate beyond node health, package state, and configuration persistence."]}
